    "# Step 4: Data Cleaning on Delta Table\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "The Customer Master data has now been loaded into a Delta Table. Before performing incremental processing, it is essential to improve the quality of the stored data.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cleaning process focuses on two major data quality issues identified during profiling:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Handling missing (null) values\n",
    "- Removing duplicate customer records\n",
    "\n",
    "Performing these operations before the MERGE step ensures that the Delta Table acts as a trusted source for incremental updates.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why is Data Cleaning Important?\n",
    "\n",
    "Poor-quality data can lead to:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Incorrect customer information\n",
    "- Duplicate records after MERGE\n",
    "- Inconsistent analytics\n",
    "- Poor decision making\n",
    "\n",
    "Cleaning the Delta Table before incremental processing improves data integrity and ensures reliable downstream processing."
   ]
