   "source": [
    "# Daily Customer Changes\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Scenario\n",
    "\n",
    "Assume the Customer Master table represents yesterday's customer data.\n",
    "\n",
    "On the following day, the CRM system sends only the customer records that have changed.\n",
    "\n",
    "These changes include:\n",
    "\n",
    "• Existing customers who updated their information.\n",
    "\n",
    "• Newly registered customers.\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of processing the complete Customer Master table again, only these changed records are processed.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is called Incremental Processing and is one of the most common ETL patterns used in modern Data Engineering."
   ]
  },
