    "# Step 8 : Slowly Changing Dimension Type 2 (SCD Type 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike SCD Type 1, where existing values are overwritten, SCD Type 2 preserves the complete history of changes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Whenever a customer record changes:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The existing record is marked as inactive.\n",
    "- An end date is assigned to the old record.\n",
    "- A new record with the updated information is inserted.\n",
    "- The new record becomes the current active version.\n",
    "\n",
    "This approach is widely used in Data Warehousing where maintaining historical information is important for reporting, auditing, and analytics."
   ]
  },
