    "# Step 9 : Comparison between SCD Type 1 and SCD Type 2\n",
    "\n",
    "After implementing both Slowly Changing Dimension techniques, the following comparison highlights their differences.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature | SCD Type 1 | SCD Type 2 |\n",
    "|----------|------------|------------|\n",
    "| History Preservation | No |  Yes |\n",
    "| Existing Record | Overwritten | Expired |\n",
    "| New Record | Not Created | Created |\n",
    "| Storage Requirement | Low | Higher |\n",
    "| Query Performance | Faster | Slightly Slower |\n",
    "| Best Use Case | Correcting Customer Details | Historical Tracking & Auditing |\n",
    "| Example | Email Update | Address History |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Observation\n",
    "\n",
    "- SCD Type 1 is suitable when only the latest information is required.\n",
    "- SCD Type 2 is preferred when maintaining historical versions of records is important.\n",
    "- In real-world Data Warehousing projects, the choice between SCD Type 1 and Type 2 depends on business requirements."
